@startuml UC-SPRINT-TASK-VIEW
' UC-24.1 - View Sprint Task | semantic key: UC-SPRINT-TASK-VIEW
' Source: data/use_cases/sprint-work/UC-SPRINT-TASK-VIEW.yml
' Business Rules: BR-PROJECT-MEMBER-ACCESS
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' One Activity Final shared by all paths (team decision 2026-10-06; UML allows one or several). It
' is reached after the Sprint Task is displayed (POST1) or after EX-01 (task no longer available,
' nothing displayed). The UC does not describe a response to EX-01, so no action is drawn (Needs
' clarification).
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|USR| $lane_title("User")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|USR|
start
' [NF1, BR-PROJECT-MEMBER-ACCESS]
:Select Sprint Task;
|SYS|
' [NF2]
:Retrieve task details, assignment,
dependencies and activity summary;
if ($question("Task still available?")) then ($guard_left("[available]"))
  ' [NF3, POST1]
  :Display Sprint Task;
else ($guard_right("[no longer", "available — EX-01]"))
endif
|SYS|
stop
@enduml
